r this question." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162297 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6e40bec4-6131-5212-9aba-bedf95289725" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162297 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162964 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186162970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162964 #edb/ref 1061 33902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162964 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1f2e7312-035a-58f0-a5f4-a7a2cb453deb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162964 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186163271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162970 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186163003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162970 #edb/ref 1061 33933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162970 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b6d57cdd-23b8-5334-ab35-b2d652c0c0d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162970 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162055 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162978 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186162979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162978 #edb/ref 1061 33983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162978 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e329fb62-17bf-50ce-9656-dcfb745d9da2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162978 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162979 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186162980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162979 #edb/ref 1061 33986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162979 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c790b092-ebdf-54f1-8b69-54a1a21f5eb3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162979 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162060 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162980 #edb/ref 1061 33988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162980 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "271cebaa-3f3c-5886-aecd-e3ab160bb06b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162980 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163003 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186162978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163003 #edb/ref 1061 34366 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163003 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7ac39654-356a-5d2e-b561-f1ca3ba76bcb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163003 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186163285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163271 #edb/ref 1064 "Let $X_1$ and $X_2$ be *independent* random variables that are normally distributed with\n\n$$\nX_1\\sim N(\\mu_1, \\sigma_1^2), \\qquad X_2\\sim N(\\mu_2, \\sigma_2^2)\n$$\n\nWe can show that the random variable\n\n$$\nY = X_1\\pm X_2\n$$\n\nis normally distributed, and\n\n$$\nY = X_1\\pm X_2 \\sim N(\\mu_1\\pm\\mu_2, \\sigma_1^2+\\sigma_2^2)\n$$\n\nWe'll prove this in a separate lesson.\n\nFor example, if $X_1\\sim N(2,3)$ and $X_2\\sim N(1,4)$ are independent, then\n\n$$\nX_{1} + X_{2} \\mid ∼N(2 + 1, 3 + 4)∼N(3, 7)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nX_{1} - X_{2} \\mid ∼N(2 - 1, 3 + 4)∼N(1, 7)\n$$\n\nWhen computing a sum or difference of normal random variables, there are a few things to watch out for:\n\n- Firstly, when we compute the distribution of a *difference*, we subtract the means, but *add* the variances!\n- Secondly, it is vital to check that $X_1$ and $X_2$ are independent. Cases where $X_1$ and $X_2$ are *dependent* will be dealt with in future lessons." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163271 #edb/ref 1065 5442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163271 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "081629c5-dd0b-5541-b151-16f392fb9a31" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163271 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163285 #edb/ref 1064 "If $X_1\\sim N(\\mu_1, \\sigma_1^2)$ and $X_2\\sim N(\\mu_2, \\sigma_2^2)$ are *independent* random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, we have\n\n$$\naX_1+bX_2\\sim N(a\\mu_1+b\\mu_2, a^2\\sigma^2_1+b^2\\sigma^2_2)\n$$\n\nFor example, if $X_1\\sim N(2,3)$ and $X_2\\sim N(1,4)$ are independent, then\n\n$$\n2X_{1} + 3X_{2} \\mid ∼N(2 \\cdot 2 + 3 \\cdot 1, 2^{2} \\cdot 3 + 3^{2} \\cdot 4); ∼N(4 + 3, 4 \\cdot 3 + 9 \\cdot 4); ∼N(7, 48)\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n2X_{1} - 3X_{2} \\mid ∼N(2 \\cdot 2 + (-3) \\cdot 1, 2^{2} \\cdot 3 + 3^{2} \\cdot 4); ∼N(4 - 3, 4 \\cdot 3 + 9 \\cdot 4); ∼N(1, 48)\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163285 #edb/ref 1065 5523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163285 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e34c3ff4-0506-5301-a7a5-0d4eea0a0ed0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163285 #edb/ref 1067 "Finding a Sum or Difference of Scaled Normal Random Variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
